WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.087
The create or replace view command lets us change a compatible view definition without dropping the view first.

00:00:08.087 --> 00:00:09.522
That sounds convenient, and it is.

00:00:09.522 --> 00:00:15.152
But do not confuse a successful command with a safe change.

00:00:15.152 --> 00:00:19.182
If we rename a column, change a data type, or change what one row represents,

00:00:19.182 --> 00:00:27.457
downstream reports may behave differently even when the database accepts the new definition.

00:00:27.457 --> 00:00:32.565
So after changing a shared view, review the contract: name, columns, types, and grain.
